ed  are you to defend yourselves and talk to  us about how the geography of the island  of taiwan gives you a a fortress of  defense anyway in the event of the  invasion that may well come from china  in the future  i think we are always  we are always  vigilant we prepared because the threat  from china it's not just overnight it's  not just last week last week or last  year it's been like that for decades  nearly 70 years  uh people like me grew up have been  growing up uh in in this kind of uh uh  uh  sort of a hemisphere that we have to be  ready all the time  uh so now uh  definitely we need to build up continue  to build up shore up our deterrence  capabilities hardware and all those and  then we are now also  looking at the possibility of  reserve  reform things like that and also there  have been a  voluntary uh  sort of a civilian defense training  among the people and these these are  good signs because basically proves that  people of taiwan are determined to  defend our sovereignty and the way our  life uh  our way of life i have a couple more  questions where you don't have end of  time i do want to try and get these  these two in  on in that in in terms of  of making sure that you have the the  relevant uh munitions to defend yourself  and also that the training is there  would you like to see more help from  britain in doing that do you know that  we've been training  yes i certainly do but not necessarily  in the sense that you were mentioning  about the efforts the uk has been put  with regard to you to to ukraine uh i i  think uh  important thing is to to boost uh the  necessary relevant uh cooperation in in  uh  in those strategic sectors  uh of course defense industry is is is  is broad  uh  and and there is definitely  opportunities for both sides to to  cooperate uh and uh i think we're pretty  much on the right track uh because uh  the uk uh we noticed that uh it's  uh it's been told it's been implementing  this still two percent indo-pacific 